    "introduction": "Standard Chartered provides banking services with a strong focus on Asia, Africa and the Middle East. It serves companies and institutions through trade finance, payments, lending and capital-markets services, alongside wealth and retail banking. Its international network is useful to clients moving goods, capital and investment across borders. Revenue comes from interest and financial-service fees, with performance influenced by borrowing demand, transaction volumes and market conditions. Customer deposits and other funding support its lending activities. Operating across diverse economies brings opportunities and complexity, making credit assessment, currency management, compliance and local market knowledge central to the business.",
